1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:03,131
Meet Cue, your AI livestream producer.

2
00:00:03,131 --> 00:00:11,396
Plan your show, connect your studio, and bring your audience into the action, all from one desktop workspace.

3
00:00:12,421 --> 00:00:14,245
Start with a simple brief.

4
00:00:14,245 --> 00:00:18,664
We're planning a city walk where chat picks the next challenge.

5
00:00:18,664 --> 00:00:22,452
Choose a director style, then create your stream plan.

6
00:00:23,465 --> 00:00:26,870
Cue turns the brief into an editable running order.

7
00:00:26,870 --> 00:00:32,010
Refine your title, category, tags, and timed segments before the show begins.

8
00:00:33,507 --> 00:00:37,951
Connect Twitch and OBS, then stage the Cue overlay in your scene.

9
00:00:37,951 --> 00:00:44,513
This walkthrough uses Demo Mode to demonstrate the workflow without starting a public broadcast.

10
00:00:45,556 --> 00:00:50,650
Run the readiness check, review the confirmation, and start the session.

11
00:00:50,650 --> 00:00:56,098
Cue keeps broadcast controls explicit, so you decide when the show goes live.

12
00:00:57,104 --> 00:00:59,106
Now chat asks for a challenge.

13
00:00:59,106 --> 00:01:03,509
Cue spots the repeated topic and turns it into an audience prompt.

14
00:01:03,509 --> 00:01:08,714
The director feed shows the supporting messages, the decision, and the result.

15
00:01:12,158 --> 00:01:13,491
You stay in control.

16
00:01:13,491 --> 00:01:21,353
Pause the director at any time to stop automatic cues, then resume when you're ready to bring chat back into the show.

17
00:01:22,445 --> 00:01:29,648
When you're done, end the session and export a recap of your production actions and highlight suggestions.

18
00:01:29,648 --> 00:01:29,920
Cue.

19
00:01:29,920 --> 00:01:31,687
Your stream, right on cue.
